  "practice": [
    "Say ঢ three times with a puff of air: ḍhô, ḍhô, ḍhô.",
    "Practice the vowel forms: ঢ (ḍhô), ঢা (ḍha), ঢি (ḍhi), ঢী (ḍhi, uncommon), ঢু (ḍhu), ঢূ (ḍhu, rare), ঢে (ḍhe), ঢৈ (ḍhoi, rare), ঢো (ḍho), and ঢৌ (ḍhou, rare).",
    "Read the combinations aloud: ঢ + া = ঢা as in ঢাকা, ঢ + ি = ঢি as in ঢিলা, ঢ + ু = ঢু as in ঢুকা, ঢ + ে = ঢে as in ঢেউ, and ঢ + ো = ঢো as in ঢোকা.",
    "Curl the tongue slightly backward and compare ড (ḍ) with ঢ (ḍh, extra air): ডাল / ঢাল, ডাক / ঢাকা, and ডিম / ঢোকা.",
    "Practice the useful verb family: ঢোকা, ঢুকছি, ঢুকতে, ঢুকে, and ঢুকবেন না.",
    "Use ঢাকা, ঢাকনা, ঢালা, ঢেউ, ঢোকা, ঢুকতে, ঢিলা, and ঢোল as quick reading anchors."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ঢ is a Bangla consonant named ḍhô. Its sound is roughly dh with the tongue curled slightly backward.",
    "ঢ is the aspirated partner of ড: the tongue position is similar, but ঢ has an extra puff of air.",
    "Compare ডাল (ḍal, lentils), ডাক (ḍak, call/mail), and ডিম (ḍim, egg) with ঢাল (ḍhal, slope/shield), ঢাকা (ḍhaka, Dhaka), and ঢোকা (ḍhoka, to enter).",
    "Best words to memorize include ঢাকা, ঢাকনা, ঢালা, ঢেউ, ঢোকা, ঢুকা, ঢুকে, ঢুকানো, ঢেকে, ঢিলা, ঢাল, ঢোল, ঢাক, ঢেঁড়স, and ঢেকুর."
